      "content": "that's what i've been trying to do but it's hard because the messages look so much like me. it's like they have all my slang and my specific way of typing. but i felt this weird chill when i saw a post from my brother today. he was replying to a comment i supposedly made, but i don't remember ever saying that thing. it sounded like a \"best version\" of me, you know? like an AI version of my personality that's just... more polished. do you think it's actually possible for an AI to have scraped enough of my data to mimic my actual \"essence\" and not just my words?",
